# Documentation chain of custody

- Independent review reports are immutable evidence.
- Do not modify a review report after the reviewer commits it.
- Corrections must use a new correction backlog, implementation report and
  correction-review report.
- Preserve superseded CI runs and earlier verdicts.
- Do not erase an incorrect prior report; record the correction separately.
- Do not mark findings independently verified based on Cursor's own tests.
- Cursor status language:
  "Implementation complete — pending independent verification"
  or
  "Correction implemented — pending independent verification"
- Only ChatGPT may record technical acceptance.
- Only the user may authorize merge.
- PROJECT_STATUS.md must reflect the live repository state, not a planned state.
- Review and implementation SHAs must be derived from Git.